# Thothly — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` before running `docker-compose up`:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# The MVP needs no API keys: YouTube uses native subtitles and blogs are
# read via RSS/scraping. Everything below has a sensible default.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional PostHog product analytics
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=<your_posthog_project_token>
# POSTHOG_HOST=<your_posthog_host>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Data directory (SQLite DB + generated EPUBs)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Inside Docker Compose the backend container mounts ./data at /data,
# so the default value below is correct and you do NOT need to set it.
# Override when running the backend directly on your host:
# DATA_DIR=./data
DATA_DIR=/data

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend URL (frontend → backend)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Override only if you run the frontend outside Docker Compose
# (e.g. `pnpm dev` on your host pointing at a remote backend).
# Inside docker-compose this is set to http://backend:8000 via the
# compose file and you do NOT need to set it here.
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Web article search
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# No setting picks the engine. With TREG_TOKEN or MONID_API_KEY set (see below),
# web search goes to TinyFish (free), with Exa as its fallback. With neither key
# it uses Marginalia: keyless, indexes the independent "small web" (blogs, docs,
# long-form). The "public" key needs no signup but shares a tight rate limit;
# request a free personal key (email contact@marginalia-search.com) for
# headroom. Free keys are CC-BY-NC-SA (NON-commercial); a paid key lifts that.
#
# MARGINALIA_API_KEY=public

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional hosted YouTube transcripts (treg -> ScrapeCreators)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube blocks subtitle fetches from datacenter IPs. On a hosted server, set a
# treg agent token (https://treg.to, `treg org agent-new <name> --cap 500`) and
# transcripts come from ScrapeCreators instead (~$0.004 per video, cached).
# Leave empty at home: yt-dlp works free from a residential IP.
# TREG_TOKEN=
#
# Monid (https://monid.ai) is the fallback gateway for the same vendor calls when
# treg is down or out of balance. Either key alone also switches web search to
# TinyFish and Exa, and enables published podcast transcripts: a selected episode
# is looked up in Exa's podcast index (~$0.007) before any speech-to-text runs.
# MONID_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional LLM cleanup (transcript re-punctuation, copyedit, …)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave these EMPTY to keep Thothly fully zero-LLM (the default): punctuated
# captions are split into clean paragraphs for free, raw captions fall back to
# naive grouping. Set all three to enable "AI polish" (and its extras) in the
# review screen. One OpenAI-compatible endpoint covers every
# provider — just point base_url + model (+ key when the provider needs one).
#
# Local & free, with Ollama (`ollama pull llama3.1`):
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
# (no LLM_API_KEY needed)
#
# Mistral:
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# LLM_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# OpenAI:
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# OpenRouter (what the public demo runs; reasoning is switched off for you).
# The same key also turns on search triage, see below:
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# LLM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl:free
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# Tried in order when the model above fails or hits the free tier's limit
# (OpenRouter only, never applied to a visitor's own key):
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODELS=["deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash"]

# Users can also bring their own key from the browser, for a provider on the
# allowlist in backend/app/pipeline/providers.py. Set this to true to also
# accept any server address they type (their own Ollama, vLLM). Only on an
# instance whose users you trust: the server calls whatever address is given.
# BYOK_ALLOW_CUSTOM_BASE_URL=false

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional speech-to-text (podcast episodes → transcript)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave these EMPTY to keep Thothly transcription-free: podcast episodes are
# then skipped (like a video with no subtitles), and many podcasts are anyway
# mirrored on YouTube, where native subtitles already cover them for free.
# Set all three to turn audio-only episodes into chapters. Same OpenAI-compatible
# shape as the LLM block — point base_url + model at any audio/transcriptions
# endpoint. An episode goes in one request when it fits under STT_MAX_CHUNK_MINUTES
# (55 by default); longer ones are split, which needs `ffmpeg` installed.
#
# Mistral Voxtral (recommended):
# STT_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# STT_MODEL=voxtral-mini-latest
# STT_API_KEY=...
#
# Local & free (vLLM serving Voxtral-Mini-3B, or a whisper.cpp server):
# STT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# STT_MODEL=voxtral-mini
# (no STT_API_KEY needed)
#
# Tuning (defaults shown):
# STT_MAX_CHUNK_MINUTES=55
# Ask the provider to label speakers (Voxtral):
# STT_DIARIZE=true
# With an LLM set, name the speakers from the dialogue:
# PODCAST_SPEAKER_NAMING=true

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Cost estimate (review screen only; Thothly never bills anything)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults track Mistral. Match them to your provider so the estimate holds.
# STT_PRICE_PER_MINUTE=0.003
# LLM_PRICE_PER_MTOK_IN=0.20
# LLM_PRICE_PER_MTOK_OUT=0.60

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Search triage (re-orders search results)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# No key of its own: when LLM_BASE_URL points at OpenRouter, the same
# LLM_API_KEY runs a decision model (Perplexity Decider v1.2) that judges every
# search result (compilable, relevant) and re-orders the list. With any other
# LLM provider, or none, results stay untriaged.
